      "reason": "This remains one structural ion-exchange competence. Fixed framework charge and mobile counterions explain 1Ca2+:2Na+ exchange, finite site capacity, competition and conditional regeneration. The given 2g×1mmol/g capacity binds 2mmol Ca2+, leaves 1mmol and releases 4mmol Na+. Fresh Mg2+ competition cannot determine exact Ca/Mg allocation without selectivity data. Lower Al at equal pore size need not preserve charge capacity. Acid neutralisation and destruction of calcium are correctly excluded. No biological degradation mastery is inferred."
